17:["$","p","1",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Healthcare privacy failures are rarely dramatic. They are screens, conversations, papers, and curiosity. The clinical staff who handle patients all day have more opportunities to breach privacy than anyone in the building."}]
18:["$","figure","2",{"children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-gray-200","children":["$","table",null,{"className":"w-full text-left border-collapse","children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"className":"bg-gray-50","children":[["$","th","0",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Situation"}],["$","th","1",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Risk"}],["$","th","2",{"scope":"col","className":"px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200","children":"Practice"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","0",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Workstation left unlocked"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Anyone passing can read the record"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Lock the screen every time you step away"}]]}],["$","tr","1",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Corridor conversations"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Overheard by patients and visitors"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Discuss patients only where you cannot be overheard"}]]}],["$","tr","2",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Calling patients from the waiting room"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Announcing more than a name"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Use the name only; never the reason for the visit"}]]}],["$","tr","3",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Printed schedules and labels"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Left visible or discarded intact"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Keep face-down; shred rather than bin"}]]}],["$","tr","4",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Curiosity about a known person"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Access without a work reason"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Never look. Access is logged and audited"}]]}],["$","tr","5",{"className":"even:bg-gray-50/50","children":[["$","td","0",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Sharing logins"}],["$","td","1",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Actions attributed to the wrong person"}],["$","td","2",{"className":"px-4 py-3 text-gray-700 border-b border-gray-100 align-top leading-relaxed","children":"Never, under any circumstances"}]]}]]}]]}]}],["$","figcaption",null,{"className":"text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 italic","children":"Everyday privacy risks"}]]}]
19:["$","p","3",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Releasing records to anyone other than for treatment, payment, or operations generally requires a valid written authorization from the patient specifying what is released, to whom, and for how long. Family members are not automatically entitled to information, and a spouse asking about a patient's visit has no inherent right to it."}]
1a:["$","div","4",{"className":"p-4 rounded-xl border-l-4 text-gray-800 leading-relaxed bg-yellow-50 border-yellow-400","children":[false,"Accessing a record you have no work reason to see is a violation even if you tell nobody and change nothing. Every access is logged and audits are routine. Looking up a friend, a neighbour, a coworker, or a family member out of concern is among the most common causes of termination in healthcare — and concern is not an exception in the rule."]}]
1b:["$","$L1f","5",{"block":{"type":"knowledge-check","question":"A patient's spouse calls asking how the appointment went. There is no authorization on file. What do you do?","options":["Give a general summary, since they are immediate family","Confirm the appointment happened but withhold clinical details","Explain that you cannot share information without the patient's authorization, and offer to have the patient contact them","Ask the provider whether it is acceptable to share"],"correctIndex":2,"explanation":"Marriage does not confer a right to another adult's health information. Without authorization, you cannot disclose clinical details — and confirming that the patient was seen at all is itself protected information. Decline politely and direct them to the patient.","optionRationales":["Family relationship alone does not authorize disclosure of an adult patient's information.","Confirming the patient was seen discloses that they received care here, which is protected on its own.","Correct. Decline without authorization and route them back to the patient.","The provider cannot authorize a disclosure the patient has not permitted. This delays the same answer."]}}]
1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-12","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3","children":"Challenge"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-lg text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"Apply what you've learned in this lesson."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-md border border-gray-200 p-8","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","p","0",{"className":"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed","children":"Audit the environment you are in."}],["$","ol","1",{"start":"$undefined","className":"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-3 text-gray-700 marker:font-semibold marker:text-primary-600","children":[["$","li","0",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"In any workplace or public setting, identify three ways private information could be observed by someone passing through. Do not record any actual information."}],["$","li","1",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Research what a valid HIPAA authorization for release of records must contain. List the required elements."}],["$","li","2",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"For each, decide whether it is a permitted disclosure: sending records to a referred specialist; telling a patient's employer they were seen; giving results to a parent of a 15-year-old; discussing a case with the treating provider."}],["$","li","3",{"className":"leading-relaxed pl-1","children":"Write a two-sentence script for declining a family member's request for information, that is firm without being cold."}]]}]]}]}]]}]
